# Extracted from IBM's SDK by tools/extract.sh and tools/extract-langs.sh.
# The language data in lang/ is in the tree, the rules as text among it, so
# nothing here is needed to build.
analysis/
build/
.wine/
result
result-*
__pycache__/

# Every form of a language's rules that a build makes rather than holds.
#
# delta_rules_<tag>.c, delta_rules_<tag>.h and delta_rules_shim_<tag>.c are
# the rules as the engine runs them -- the bytecode array, the header
# numbering every entry, and a shim under each rule's own name -- written out
# of lang/<tag>/rules by `make rulecode', which every build runs first, and
# about two seconds a language. The text is the source; a second copy of the
# same rules in the tree could only ever be the stale one.
#
# delta_rules_cNN_<tag>.c is those rules decompiled into C, thirteen
# megabytes of it by tools/delta-decompile.py, rewritten whole by every
# change to that tool. `make rules' makes them. Numbered because one
# translation unit that size cannot be compiled on more than one core.
lang/*/delta_rules_*.c
lang/*/delta_rules_*.h
# Except the empty table that leaves every rule as bytecode, which is written
# by hand once per language and is generated from nothing.
!lang/*/delta_rules_none_*.c
# And except Japanese's three, which are the exception docs/japanese.md gives:
# that module has no rules as text for a build to compile, `tools/rules/emit.py'
# writes these straight out of IBM's objects, and they are therefore the only
# copy there is. The decompiled form is still made rather than held.
!lang/jajp/delta_rules_jajp.c
!lang/jajp/delta_rules_jajp.h
!lang/jajp/delta_rules_shim_jajp.c

# The default output name of cli/probe.c and reference/speak.c, so it
# appears in the root whenever either is run without one.
speak.wav
